      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>When set, indicates that this Call does not actually exist locally for the ConnectionService.</para>
          <para>Consider, for example, a scenario where a user has two phones with the same phone number. When a user places a call on one device, the telephony stack can represent that call on the other device by adding it to the ConnectionService with the Connection.PROPERTY_IS_EXTERNAL_CALL property set.</para>
          <para>An InCallService will only see calls with this property if it has the TelecomManager.METADATA_INCLUDE_EXTERNAL_CALLS metadata set to true in its manifest.</para>
          <para>See Connection.PROPERTY_IS_EXTERNAL_CALL.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/telecom/Call.Details#PROPERTY_IS_EXTERNAL_CALL" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.telecom.Call.Details.PROPERTY_IS_EXTERNAL_CALL</code>.</a></format></para>
